{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_document", "label": "React Native Performance Reference", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Profile a release build on a low or mid-range physical device. Change one thing and measure again. Dev builds, simulators, and flagship phones hide the problem."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_flashlist", "label": "FlashList", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Lists", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prefer FlashList recycling. Provide estimatedItemSize on v1 and getItemType for mixed rows. Do not put key on the row root inside renderItem, because that breaks recycling. Local row state must handle being reset when the row is recycled. The trade-off is that FlashList needs size hints."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_flatlist", "label": "FlatList", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Lists", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use stable IDs in keyExtractor, never the index for a mutable list. Use getItemLayout for fixed heights, initialNumToRender about one screen, windowSize 5 to 9 because the default 21 is memory heavy, maxToRenderPerBatch about 8 to 10, and updateCellsBatchingPeriod about 50. removeClippedSubviews on Android can leave blank items, so test it."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_scrollview", "label": "ScrollView", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Lists", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not nest vertical lists inside a ScrollView. Use ListHeaderComponent or SectionList. Do not load thousands of rows into state; paginate onEndReached around a 0.5 threshold with an in-flight guard."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_section_list", "label": "SectionList", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Lists", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SectionList replaces a nested vertical list inside a ScrollView when rows are grouped."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_memo", "label": "React.memo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Re-renders", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fix re-renders in this order: move state down, split components, select with shallow equality, then React.memo with stable props, then useMemo and useCallback. Keep text-input state local and lift it on submit or debounce, not on each keystroke."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_reanimated", "label": "Reanimated", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Animation & gestures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drive shared values and useAnimatedStyle so animation stays on the UI thread. Do not call setState inside onScroll or gesture callbacks; use shared values or useAnimatedScrollHandler. Animate transform and opacity only."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_gesture_handler", "label": "Gesture Handler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Animation & gestures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gestures go through Gesture Handler so they run on the UI thread with Reanimated, instead of bouncing through the JS thread."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_layout_animation", "label": "LayoutAnimation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Animation & gestures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LayoutAnimation and animating width or height relayout every frame. Core Animated must set useNativeDriver and still cannot animate layout props."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_expo_image", "label": "expo-image", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Images", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use disk and memory cache, contentFit, and blurhash or thumbhash placeholders, and always pass width and height. Decoded bitmap memory is about width times height times 4 bytes, so a 4000 by 3000 photo is about 48MB. Prefetch only what is about to show. Prefer WebP or AVIF."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_native_svg", "label": "react-native-svg", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Images", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Many SVG nodes are expensive on the UI thread. Flatten paths, avoid hundreds of SVGs in a list, and rasterize static ones."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_lottie", "label": "Lottie", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Animation & gestures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prefer small Lottie or vector assets, and disable animation when AccessibilityInfo.isReduceMotionEnabled is true."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_hermes", "label": "Hermes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keep Hermes enabled. Release builds use precompiled bytecode. Its sampling profiler, opened in Chrome DevTools from a .cpuprofile, is the main JS CPU tool."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_new_architecture", "label": "New Architecture", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fabric, TurboModules, and JSI remove the async bridge, so native calls can be synchronous with less serialization. On by default at React Native 0.76 or newer. Confirm each native dependency with expo-doctor or release notes. Libraries stuck on the old bridge can get slower through the interop layer."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_fabric", "label": "Fabric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fabric is the New Architecture renderer. It is part of dropping the async bridge."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_turbomodules", "label": "TurboModules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TurboModules are the New Architecture native-module system. Synchronous native calls avoid the old bridge serialization cost."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_jsi", "label": "JSI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JSI is how the New Architecture makes native calls synchronous. CPU-heavy crypto should move to a JSI or native module instead of pure JS."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_inline_requires", "label": "inlineRequires", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Startup time", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Set transformer.getTransformOptions inlineRequires in metro.config.js so modules load on first use. Do not import crypto, wallet, charts, or PDF at the top of App.tsx."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_devtools_profiler", "label": "React DevTools Profiler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Record a commit and inspect why a component rendered. Highlight updates shows extra renders. Use it when there are too many renders or slow commits."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_perf_monitor", "label": "Perf Monitor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The in-app Perf Monitor shows JS FPS and UI FPS separately. Low JS FPS means JS-bound. Low UI FPS means native or draw-bound."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_android_studio_profiler", "label": "Android Studio Profiler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use it for Android CPU, memory heap dumps, and startup profiling, next to Profile GPU rendering."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_xcode_instruments", "label": "Xcode Instruments", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On iOS use Time Profiler, Allocations, Core Animation, and Leaks. Allocations and Leaks cover memory."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_dumpsys_gfxinfo", "label": "dumpsys gfxinfo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo framestats reports Android frame stats."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_bundle_visualizer", "label": "react-native-bundle-visualizer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npx react-native-bundle-visualizer shows which packages dominate the JS bundle. The top few packages are usually the problem."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_source_map_explorer", "label": "source-map-explorer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "source-map-explorer is the other named way to inspect bundle size from source maps."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_expo_export", "label": "expo export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "npx expo export, including a dumped source map, is how exported bundle output sizes are inspected."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_native_quick_crypto", "label": "react-native-quick-crypto", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Keeping the JS thread free", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Move crypto and hashing off the JS thread with a JSI or native module such as react-native-quick-crypto instead of a pure-JS library, or precompute on the server. Chunk remaining work with await yields or requestAnimationFrame."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_r8_proguard", "label": "R8/ProGuard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Enable R8, ProGuard, and resource shrinking in release, and ship an AAB with per-ABI splits. Set enableProguardInReleaseBuilds. largeHeap is a last resort."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_freeze", "label": "react-freeze", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Memory", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stack screens stay mounted. Release heavy resources on blur with useFocusEffect, or use unmountOnBlur, or freeze with react-freeze and freezeOnBlur. Repeat a flow about 10 times and confirm the heap plateaus."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_react_compiler", "label": "React Compiler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Re-renders", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If babel shows the compiler is enabled, do not hand-memoize what it already handles. Keep components pure so it can optimize."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_interaction_manager", "label": "InteractionManager", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Animation & gestures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defer heavy JS with InteractionManager.runAfterInteractions so it does not run during animations. After first paint, the same API or a zero-delay setTimeout defers analytics, push registration, migrations, and network warm-up."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_moment", "label": "moment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "moment is a common bundle-size cost. Replace it with date-fns or dayjs."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_date_fns", "label": "date-fns", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lighter replacement for moment when the bundle visualizer shows date code dominating."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_dayjs", "label": "dayjs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lighter replacement for moment, alongside date-fns."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_lodash", "label": "lodash", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not import the full lodash barrel. Import lodash/xxx or use a native alternative. Import specific submodules when a library does not tree-shake."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_anr", "label": "ANR", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Android-specific tuning", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ANRs come from main-thread blocking in native code, including synchronous I/O in native modules. Low-end Android, about 3GB of RAM or less, is the real target. Persist in-progress forms and transactions because the process can be killed."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_js_thread", "label": "JS thread", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Keeping the JS thread free", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Low JS FPS means the JS thread is the bottleneck. Avoid large JSON parse or stringify, big array spreads, cascading setState from sockets, and console.log on hot paths. Batch network results into one state update, debounce search, and throttle scroll handlers."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_ui_thread", "label": "UI thread", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Profiling tools (use the right one for the bottleneck)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Low UI FPS means native or draw work. Heavy row content such as SVG, QR codes, gradients, and shadows is the usual cost. Use lightweight placeholders or cache them as images. Use elevation sparingly because shadows overdraw. Avoid stacked translucent layers."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_startup", "label": "Startup time", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Startup time", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cold start is native init plus JS bundle load plus first render plus initial data. Measure with adb shell am start -W TotalTime and WaitTime, plus Hermes console.time markers. Keep the splash only until first meaningful content, render skeletons instead of blocking on the network, and avoid synchronous storage or a large JSON.parse on startup. Polyfills run before everything, so keep them minimal."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_memory", "label": "Memory", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Memory", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Images and long lists dominate. Bound caches with an LRU, do not keep large blobs or full history in React state, lower windowSize, and size images correctly. Cancel in-flight requests and do not setState after unmount."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_expo_vector_icons", "label": "@expo/vector-icons", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Import only the icon sets you use so unused font families are not bundled. Also drop unused font weights and compress PNGs to WebP."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_babel_plugin_transform_remove_console", "label": "babel-plugin-transform-remove-console", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Bundle & app size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strip console calls in production. Keep error and warn if you still need them. console.log on a hot path is expensive in dev and leaks data in production."}, {"id": "claude_skills_react_native_dev_references_performance_expo_doctor", "label": "expo-doctor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/react-native-dev/references/performance.md", "source_location": "Hermes & New Architecture", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use expo-doctor, 